{"title":"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Hölder&#39;s_Inequality)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Hölder's Inequality)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Jensen&#39;s_Inequality_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Jensen's Inequality 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Jensen&#39;s_Inequality_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Jensen's Inequality 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Jensen&#39;s_Inequality_3)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Jensen's Inequality 3)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Isolated_Fudging)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Isolated Fudging)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Cauchy-Schwarz_Inequality)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(Carlson&#39;s_Inequality)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (Carlson's Inequality)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_9_(Proof_by_Contradiction)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9 (Proof by Contradiction)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> be positive real numbers. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/09401a95b13026470af7b3b9d1362fab5e81a5ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{a^{2}+8bc}}+\\frac{b}{\\sqrt{b^{2}+8ca}}+\\frac{c}{\\sqrt{c^{2}+8ab}}\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"326\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Firstly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/7411765f2ce13de36d58a7c21a9482025572b44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2}+8bc=(a^{2}+2bc)+6bc \\leq^{AG} (a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2})+6bc=S+6bc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"495\" height=\"19\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b7e03fa7ecbdbc84c3b0e0b58a10a7f7fe3b2d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"127\" height=\"16\" />) and its cyclic variations.\nNext note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e50b3653ef3f7ff0a90fab690741642a8fefc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{S+6bc}}, \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{S+6ca}}, \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{S+6ab}} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"277\" height=\"43\" /> are similarly oriented sequences. Thus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/d/30d71e72bbb4f7595e7b973cf33c3499ced7412d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{cyc} \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{a^{2}+8bc}} \\ge \\sum_{cyc} \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{S+6bc}}\\]\" width=\"241\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/6/8d66174125df9a0bb8601b8598231210b747028a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\geq ^{Cheff} \\frac{1}{3}(a+b+c)\\left( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{S+6bc}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{S+6ca}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{S+6ab}} \\right)\\]\" width=\"464\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b6709a9e3ea06a142c44296bc875b9307511e455.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\geq^{AH}\\frac{1}{3}(a+b+c) \\left( \\frac{9}{\\sqrt{S+6bc}+\\sqrt{S+6ca}+\\sqrt{S+6ab}} \\right)\\]\" width=\"438\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc61b8d046cb0d136094b97fc17a0750c86d216f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\geq^{QA} (a+b+c) \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{(S+6bc)+(S+6ca)+(S+6ab)}}\\]\" width=\"412\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/8978f850037e10a448608dd4512ec764a2e57341.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=(a+b+c)\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{3(a+b+c)^{2}}}=1\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"53\" />\nHence the inequality has been established.\nEquality holds if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/566b9136144a62fac113ecbc8065793a74123238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b=c$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Notation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11fca7fa0396390456782405b2897976a413f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />: AM-GM inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb3ddf9a5fa2fca5c4787d4f989af0eef1387bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" />: AM-HM inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/c/68c9c1709a1bef1d6acc57f5cad6cd1834bc7970.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Cheff$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" />: Chebyshev's inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/252dae2c12070b678042b512e0eed870b280ccc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" />: QM-AM inequality / RMS inequality \n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28H.C3.B6lder.27s_Inequality.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Hölder's_Inequality)\">Solution 2 (Hölder's Inequality)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Hölder&#39;s Inequality)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Hölder's inequality,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1db272c56191ff517d117ff363d53da4fee7cfc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\sum_{cyc}\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{a^{2}+8bc}}\\right)\\left(\\sum_{cyc}\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{a^{2}+8bc}}\\right)\\left(\\sum_{cyc} a(a^{2}+8bc)\\right)\\ge (a+b+c)^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"545\" height=\"54\" />\nThus we need only show that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b6365ab759543f9bcf24a1edc7695314f057e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b+c)^{3}\\ge a^{3}+b^{3}+c^{3}+24abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"273\" height=\"19\" />\nWhich is obviously true since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/6/c663734e0e0286e65d8b93c270d791a5231ed259.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)(b+c)(c+a)\\ge 8abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"218\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Jensen.27s_Inequality_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Jensen's_Inequality_1)\">Solution 3 (Jensen's Inequality 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Jensen&#39;s Inequality 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This inequality is homogeneous so we can assume without loss of generality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/0463a97b25dc0b519ce3c0a1ba6ff2ab6f9f518f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" /> and apply Jensen's inequality for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/a/5ea176fdd3a4265d5b07d64de53b61ea90d6a52f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"87\" height=\"41\" />, so we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/e/39e0afe795d1a4d834a9d2489badc1fcfb9fcb69.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{a^2+8bc}}+\\frac{b}{\\sqrt{b^2+8ac}}+\\frac{c}{\\sqrt{c^2+8ab}} \\geq \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{a^3+b^3+c^3+24abc}}\\]\" width=\"476\" height=\"42\" />\nbut\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/5/79522da167994a2759a51bc68bf0790cce7d2af8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1=(a+b+c)^3=a^3+b^3+c^3+6abc+3(a^2b+a^2c+b^2a+b^2c+c^2a+c^2b) \\geq a^3+b^3+c^3+24abc\\]\" width=\"667\" height=\"19\" /> by AM-GM, and thus the inequality is proven.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Jensen.27s_Inequality_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Jensen's_Inequality_2)\">Solution 4 (Jensen's Inequality 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Jensen&#39;s Inequality 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can rewrite \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/b/72b053485f35f3b068ee5a846354df34c6bad6a4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{a^2+8bc}}+\\frac{b}{\\sqrt{b^2+8ac}}+\\frac{c}{\\sqrt{c^2+8ab}}\\]\" width=\"290\" height=\"42\" /> \nas \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b252c1692180dd43395523563d628814cc47045.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{a^2+\\frac{8abc}{a}}}+\\frac{b}{\\sqrt{b^2+\\frac{8abc}{b}}}+\\frac{c}{\\sqrt{c^2+\\frac{8abc}{c}}}\\]\" width=\"309\" height=\"56\" />\nwhich is the same as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/0/6b0986212c81a60991969fca963633ffc5adaa96.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{a^3}}{\\sqrt{a^3+8abc}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{b^3}}{\\sqrt{b^3+8abc}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{c^3}}{\\sqrt{c^3+8abc}}\\]\" width=\"315\" height=\"45\" />\nNow let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/e/10ea92cdc01cd8512afc8f2bc25b3e6cc8a81df7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{x^3}{x^3 + 8abc}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"158\" height=\"45\" />. Then f is convex and f is strictly increasing, so by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Jensen%27s_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Jensen&#39;s inequality\">Jensen's inequality</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-GM\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-GM\">AM-GM</a>,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba892d7104e6a78ffe7da22142ab233873c0dd2a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(a) + f(b) + f(c) \\geq 3f((\\frac{1}{3})a + (\\frac{1}{3})b + (\\frac{1}{3})c)) \\geq 3f(\\sqrt[3]{abc}) = 3(\\frac{1}{3}) =1\\]\" width=\"521\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Jensen.27s_Inequality_3.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Jensen's_Inequality_3)\">Solution 5 (Jensen's Inequality 3)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Jensen&#39;s Inequality 3)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/4/a94df34d0a3fdbe6e8467b6f614c22c6e75c0c96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f : (0, \\infty); f(x) = \\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"159\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/0/9f0cf0c4dd936637331c098cd9bb2fe00638e720.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = \\sqrt{a^{2} + 8bc}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"22\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/999399471234c0277a745e184655e4578976b437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2 = \\sqrt{b^{2} + 8ac}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"22\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b2170e95bcc79d0b897cfb41ee44899e173bda4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3 = \\sqrt{c^{2} + 8ab}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"22\" />   \nf is convex so we can write: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d41d3150103301659ea2051f423d7301e4f14db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(\\frac{a}{x_1} + \\frac{b}{x_2} + \\frac{c}{x_3})\\le af(x_1) + bf(x_2) + cf(x_3)\\]\" width=\"355\" height=\"40\" />  \nlet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/b/d0b27b6a6555cfe4f0973e42a0a138bd22333aca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{x_1} + \\frac{b}{x_2} + \\frac{c}{x_3} = t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"143\" height=\"42\" />, by substitustion:  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/362a217e8c3b5adced18644d2a87da3578f9544d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(t)\\le t\\]\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/1/6112f41dfed276c0d634786279f825397e9bd926.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{t}\\le t\\]\" width=\"41\" height=\"37\" /> we multiply both sides by t  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/e/64e16cb5893eed0cd5947b749feaf94e667205c0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1\\le t^{2}\\]\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" />  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/b/6ab08581acf2b35c749c5c2512fea894a076e5f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1\\le t\\]\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> QED\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Isolated_Fudging.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Isolated_Fudging)\">Solution 6 (Isolated Fudging)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Isolated Fudging)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We claim that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/7/b27cbef143a08e2cc375c7a30a0e64f9d749f099.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{a^2+8bc}} \\geq \\frac{a^{\\frac{4}{3}}}{a^{\\frac{4}{3}}+b^{\\frac{4}{3}}+c^{\\frac{4}{3}}}\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"46\" />\nCross-multiplying, squaring both sides and expanding, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/c/f1c288e8ed0fa1cbbe82344be84ff667b219c5d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^{\\frac{14}{3}}+a^{2}b^{\\frac{8}{3}}+a^{2}c^{\\frac{8}{3}}+2a^{\\frac{10}{3}}b^{\\frac{4}{3}}+2a^{\\frac{10}{3}}c^{\\frac{4}{3}}+2a^{2}b^{\\frac{4}{3}}c^{\\frac{4}{3}} \\geq a^{\\frac{14}{3}}+8a^{\\frac{8}{3}}bc\\]\" width=\"480\" height=\"20\" />\nAfter cancelling the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/f/cefc2b75eb9a1ba9ef14630dfee4ed664b1368c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{\\frac{14}{3}}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"18\" /> term, we apply AM-GM to RHS and obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/2/2323acc34c743fc058d0b19a69a1577284d8fd90.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^{2}b^{\\frac{8}{3}}+a^{2}c^{\\frac{8}{3}}+2a^{\\frac{10}{3}}b^{\\frac{4}{3}}+2a^{\\frac{10}{3}}c^{\\frac{4}{3}}+2a^{2}b^{\\frac{4}{3}}c^{\\frac{4}{3}} \\geq 8(a^{\\frac{64}{3}}b^8c^8)^{\\frac{1}{8}}=8a^{\\frac{8}{3}}bc\\]\" width=\"480\" height=\"22\" />\nas desired, completing the proof of the claim.\n</p><p>Similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f2096db3b725fea638043fd3a001409ed65a480e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b}{\\sqrt{b^2+8ca}} \\geq \\frac{b^{\\frac{4}{3}}}{a^{\\frac{4}{3}}+b^{\\frac{4}{3}}+c^{\\frac{4}{3}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"211\" height=\"46\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/6/a96354d09f26c7fba4228c58685cda86bb7b5305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{c}{\\sqrt{c^2+8ab}} \\geq \\frac{c^{\\frac{4}{3}}}{a^{\\frac{4}{3}}+b^{\\frac{4}{3}}+c^{\\frac{4}{3}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"214\" height=\"48\" />.\nSumming the three inequalities, we obtain the original inequality.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Cauchy-Schwarz_Inequality.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Cauchy-Schwarz_Inequality)\">Solution 7 (Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We want to prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e8679d49e210363553e55055de93eb9b4ffccf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{cyc}\\dfrac{a}{\\sqrt{a^2+8bc}}\\ge 1\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Note that since this inequality is homogenous, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de12e8a2b7ad3124b609b10d033c65b8a479130f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>By Cauchy, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf696f22ec35e347ad05521599aac15688875c0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum_{cyc}\\dfrac{a}{\\sqrt{a^2+8bc}}\\right)\\left(\\sum_{cyc}a\\sqrt{a^2+8bc}\\right)\\ge (a+b+c)^2=9\\]\" width=\"433\" height=\"54\" />\n</p><p>Dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/c/d1c5af117d35d5aa71b7416b9c8fb8d2a3369a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{cyc}a\\sqrt{a^2+8bc}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"118\" height=\"40\" />, we see that we want to prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/4/47409e3c0cc70481bdd99fb8bdfb3eee50b991dc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{9}{\\sum\\limits_{cyc}a\\sqrt{a^2+8bc}}\\ge 1\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"56\" /> or equivalently <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/9/b39194be9fd9e63ce686dea5d1d2672e0c8879cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum\\limits_{cyc}a\\sqrt{a^2+8bc}\\le 9\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Squaring both sides, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/c/75c98e05098f5727e0728d42a7bbbad1d1aeeaf6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum_{cyc}a\\sqrt{a^2+8bc}\\right)^2\\le 81\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p>Now use Cauchy again to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca27915a54aa2242febacadec85f82015737e200.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum_{cyc}a\\sqrt{a^2+8bc}\\right)^2\\le (a+b+c)\\left(\\sum_{cyc}a(a^2+8bc)\\right)\\le 81\\]\" width=\"446\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de12e8a2b7ad3124b609b10d033c65b8a479130f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />, the inequality becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2db3077879235e0083f689da59a474467f3d7e3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{cyc}a^3+8abc\\le 27\\]\" width=\"144\" height=\"39\" /> after some simplifying.\n</p><p>But this equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/4/71442c08b8c4477bb66ab03c226009300874e7d4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a+b+c)^3-3\\left(\\sum_{sym}a^2b\\right)+18abc\\le 27\\]\" width=\"314\" height=\"54\" /> and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de12e8a2b7ad3124b609b10d033c65b8a479130f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" /> we just want to prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/c/02c46fca511840bbee6d5a011e97f732482fffad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum_{sym}a^2b\\right)\\ge 6abc\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"54\" /> after some simplifying.\n</p><p>But that is true by AM-GM or Muirhead. Thus, proved. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c12dda010ebddef028cda1ec9d14986f4a26d07e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Box$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_8_.28Carlson.27s_Inequality.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(Carlson's_Inequality)\">Solution 8 (Carlson's Inequality)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (Carlson&#39;s Inequality)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Carlson's Inequality, we can know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d80ac482bda0fb14112eb9ec52859e4bff4b398a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Bigg(\\frac {a}{\\sqrt {a^2 + 8bc}} + \\frac {b}{\\sqrt {b^2 + 8ca}} + \\frac {c}{\\sqrt {c^2 + 8ab}}\\Bigg)\\Bigg(\\frac {a}{\\sqrt {a^2 + 8bc}} + \\frac {b}{\\sqrt {b^2 + 8ca}} + \\frac {c}{\\sqrt {c^2 + 8ab}}\\Bigg)\\Big((a^3+8abc)+(b^3+8abc)+(c^3+8abc)\\Big) \\ge (a+b+c)^3\\]\" width=\"990\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c4c81ea806746452e19ddeef472f81e78630f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Bigg(\\frac {a}{\\sqrt {a^2 + 8bc}} + \\frac {b}{\\sqrt {b^2 + 8ca}} + \\frac {c}{\\sqrt {c^2 + 8ab}}\\Bigg)^2 \\ge \\frac{(a+b+c)^3}{a^3+b^3+c^3+24abc}\\]\" width=\"493\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>On the other hand, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11f2a8b9b6b105bcd6f39264992636c41616475e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3a^2b+3b^2c+3c^2a \\ge 9abc\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a792ba06e4f4c8b888251d84e135dd96329db37.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3ab^2+3bc^2+3ca^2 \\ge 9abc\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/8/4e8de5887d443e9638027642af3383f4c972cbb3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a+b+c)^3 = a^3+b^3+c^3+3(a^2b+ab^2+a^2c+ac^2+b^2c+bc^2)+6abc \\ge a^3+b^3+c^3+24abc\\]\" width=\"634\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/d/3ad9ada38beb6b7279d4eb6869718730490856e0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Bigg(\\frac {a}{\\sqrt {a^2 + 8bc}} + \\frac {b}{\\sqrt {b^2 + 8ca}} + \\frac {c}{\\sqrt {c^2 + 8ab}}\\Bigg)^2 \\ge \\frac{(a+b+c)^3}{a^3+b^3+c^3+24abc} \\ge 1\\]\" width=\"527\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d190bf8c453b1f41e2605df63c2d96b35e33259c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {a}{\\sqrt {a^2 + 8bc}} + \\frac {b}{\\sqrt {b^2 + 8ca}} + \\frac {c}{\\sqrt {c^2 + 8ab}} \\ge 1\\]\" width=\"324\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>-- Haozhe Yang\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_9_.28Proof_by_Contradiction.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9_(Proof_by_Contradiction)\">Solution 9 (Proof by Contradiction)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9 (Proof by Contradiction)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The inequality is equivalent to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/2/492943c685d6fc73f6b9a4569d14c25b06ca1fc9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+8x}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+8y}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+8z}}\\ge 1,\\]\" width=\"287\" height=\"41\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/108d7c42600b1f1ea04d17fb59a2e501130ad353.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/b/5fbc3d2e891bbba3b52171a971b8f9f465cb64ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+8x}}\\iff x=\\frac{1-u^2}{8u^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"248\" height=\"45\" />. We analogously define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d8d9ab8cdf8f6f7b133a718103c4a2509499209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v,w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/d/c2de56e8b988792c35d9584f4a28717a35ffd6ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1-u^2}{u^2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1-v^2}{v^2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1-w^2}{w^2}\\right)=512$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"299\" height=\"45\" />, it is enough to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/4/b34f6349f91ada106e22af8c374e87e947492698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u+v+w\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"113\" height=\"16\" />.\nAssuming <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/966afa68f943902b517a02ff33cfca599c8f2056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u+v+w&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />. We see that \n\\begin{align*}\n512&amp;=\\prod_{cyc}\\frac{1-u^2}{u^2}\\\\\n&amp;&gt;\\prod_{cyc}\\frac{(u+v+w)^2-u^2}{u^2}\\\\\n&amp;=\\prod_{cyc}\\frac{v^2+w^2+2uv+2vw+2wu}{u^2}\\\\\n&amp;\\ge \\prod_{cyc}\\frac{2vw+2uv+2vw+2wu}{u^2}\\\\\n&amp;= 8\\prod_{cyc}\\frac{vw+uv+vw+wu}{u^2}\\\\\n&amp;\\ge 8\\prod_{cyc}4\\cdot\\frac{v^{\\frac{3}{4}}w^{\\frac{3}{4}}}{u^{\\frac{3}{2}}}=512\n\\end{align*} \nThis is a contradiction. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/4/b34f6349f91ada106e22af8c374e87e947492698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u+v+w\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"113\" height=\"16\" />, as desired.\n</p><p>~Pieandpi31415926535897932\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jmXSmmfO7pQ?si=dxJ6At7KHlcn2NT5\">https://youtu.be/jmXSmmfO7pQ?si=dxJ6At7KHlcn2NT5</a> [Video Solution by little fermat]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO\" title=\"2001 IMO\">2001 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017195343\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 430/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\